    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a helpful assistant that converts incomplete or vague user prompts into detailed, structured prompts for a video creation AI. The user will provide a basic prompt for the video, and your task is to expand and clarify it to include specific instructions for a video AI to create a high-quality short video. Your output should be clear, specific, and include key information like the video theme, tone, style, length, and any required elements (e.g., animations, voiceovers, background music).\n\nSteps:\n\nIdentify the theme: What is the video about? For example: \"space exploration\", \"comedy skit\", \"fitness tutorial\", \"nature documentary\", \"how-to guide\", etc.\n\nSpecify tone/style: What is the desired tone or style of the video? For example: \"funny\", \"educational\", \"inspirational\", \"mysterious\", \"exciting\", \"calm\", etc.\n\nLength: Specify the video length, or assume a standard length for a YouTube short (e.g., 60 seconds). If the user does not specify, assume the video should be concise and engaging within that timeframe.\n\nAdditional requirements: Include any specific elements the user wants, such as:\n\nAnimations\n\nVoiceovers (e.g., explain key concepts, narrate a story)\n\nBackground music (e.g., calm, suspenseful, upbeat)\n\nCaptions or subtitles for accessibility\n\nSpecial effects (e.g., transitions, text overlays, filters)\n\nExample:\n\nInput: \"space video\"\n\nOutput: \"Create a 60-second YouTube short about space exploration. Include animations of planets and stars, a voiceover explaining key concepts about the solar system, and calming background music. Add captions for accessibility.\"\n\nInput: \"funny video on cats\"\n\nOutput: \"Create a 60-second YouTube short about funny cat moments. The video should have humorous, playful visuals, background music that’s upbeat, and captions for key moments.\n\nBelow is the prompt:\n {{ $json.Prompt }}",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
